// T2 — A decision lands and reaches Sift, and chatter never does
// Source of record: docs/sidd/round30/pass7-domain-spec.md ("S:n" = its line n) and the accepted ADRs docs/adrs/SIFT-ADR-0*.md.
// Founder ruling 2026-11-04: Source = "Spec of record". NDD-SOURCE.md is a derived document: it gives the thread structure and the titles only; where it differs from the spec, the spec wins.
//
// STORY FLOW (founder ruling bd996f3e, 2026-11-07, "15 story flows, branches inside"): the main path runs from the start of the thread to its T2.O2 terminal, in the order the spec tells it.
// Every alternative of the thread, once a flow of its own, is a branch at the moment where it diverges: a [branch] moment that holds its deciding event as a plain node (moved from the main path, not copied), an empty first arm `TheMainPath` (the walk takes the first arm when none is chosen, so the main path is the one that goes on after the moment) and one `when` arm for each alternative,
// each ending at its own exit ([outcome] when it is a normal outcome of the thread, [terminal] for a failure or a refusal) or falling through into the moments that follow. Moment derives one scenario for each path. A refusal is a precondition of a command; Moment 0.9.0 derives its negative scenario for every path of the flow (ADR-042). A branch moment that nothing precedes (the first node of the flow, or one whose deciding event is the only node of the previous branch moment's main arm) keeps its first arm `TheMainPath` with the main path's next nodes: no event to anchor on (docs/sidd/round30/story-flows-log.md, 0.9.0 rework).
// A branch arm cites the former flow it carries in its first comment line (the old-to-new mapping is in docs/sidd/round30/story-flows-log.md).
// BRANCHES:
//   T2.M2 · The gate admits it: APointerOfAnyOtherTypeIsFiltered (former flow t2-a-pointer-of-any-other-type-is-filtered.moment)
//   T2.M2 · The gate admits it: AWriteMadeOnSiftsOwnConnectionIsNeverAdmitted (former flow t2-a-write-made-on-sifts-own-connection-is-never-admitted.moment)
//   T2.M2 · The gate admits it: PostponedWorkIsRefusedWhenSiftIsDisabledMeanwhile (former flow t2-postponed-work-is-refused-when-sift-is-disabled-meanwhile.moment)
//   T2.M2 · The gate admits it: SiftIsDisabledAndTheGateRefusesTheEntry (former flow t2-sift-is-disabled-and-the-gate-refuses-the-entry.moment)
//   T2.M2 · The gate admits it: TheWorkspaceIsNotReadySoTheWorkIsPostponed (former flow t2-the-workspace-is-not-ready-so-the-work-is-postponed.moment)
//   T2.M5 · It is read and handed on: ASessionEndsAndTheQuestionsArriveTogether (former flow t2-a-session-ends-and-the-questions-arrive-together.moment)
//   T2.M5 · It is read and handed on: TheEntryYieldsNoCandidate (former flow t2-the-entry-yields-no-candidate.moment)
//   T2.M5 · It is read and handed on: TheSourceAlreadyHasAScopeTombstone (former flow t2-the-source-already-has-a-scope-tombstone.moment)
//   T2.M7 · The unit of work is complete (continued): MarkProcessedFails (former flow t2-mark-processed-fails.moment)
// REFUSALS BY A PRECONDITION on a command of the main path (derived as negative scenarios for every path of the flow, Moment 0.9.0 ADR-042) (a derived `neg-<Command>-<Precondition>` scenario): RecordReceipt.OneReceiptPerPointer and HashSetOnce;
// DIFFERENCES FROM NDD-SOURCE (the spec wins): the NDD draws RM2 convergence after ReceiptRecorded; the spec folds ReceiptRecorded into the convergence read model only for a document version
// (S:1298), so T2.M4 has no read-model node; the NDD feed pointer "to `{ws}::sift-feed` (kinds entry, boundary, answer*)" and the guards "workspace entitled, `sift_enabled` on its META" are not in the spec.
// Part of the model directory; validate with `moment parse model/` (project mode) and `moment test` on this file.

flow "T2 — A decision lands and reaches Sift, and chatter never does"
  description "T2 — A decision lands and reaches Sift, and chatter never does. The story of the thread from its start to its T2.O2 outcome, with its alternatives as branches at the moment where each diverges. Source of record: docs/sidd/round30/pass7-domain-spec.md."

  lane flmnt "Flmnt" [External]
  lane enablement "Enablement" [Supporting]
  lane intake "Intake" [Core]
  lane design "DesignModel" [Core]

  moment "T2.M1 · A decision is recorded in flmnt"
    // [person] a person or an agent records a decision, an exploration or a keyframe in flmnt; what crosses to Sift is the Pointer, an ingress reference to an flmnt entry  // S:185 "flmnt → C2 and C4 (the feed, request and erasure streams; tenancy): Anticorruption Layer"
    note flmnt: "A person or an agent records a decision, an exploration or a keyframe in flmnt. What crosses to Sift is the Pointer, an ingress reference to an flmnt entry, never content"  // S:1181 "an ingress reference to an flmnt entry or a document section, never a pass's trigger event"

  moment "T2.M2 · The gate admits it" [branch]
    when TheMainPath
      // the main path of the story
      // The gate is not a command: when work is taken it reads the latest SiftEnabled or SiftDisabled recorded on SiftEnablement, directly, and records its decision (admitted, refused, filtered, Postponed or no-op); the decision is not declarable  // S:294 "the gate reads the latest SiftEnabled or SiftDisabled recorded on SiftEnablement, directly, and records its decision"
      // The gate runs before RecordReceipt  // S:309 "The gate runs **before** RecordReceipt."
      design: RecordGateDecision  // S:1410 "RecordGateDecision | the hard-stop gate, when work is taken"
      design: GateDecisionRecorded  // S:1352 "GateDecisionRecorded | StartCycle (an Admitted decision starts the Cycle)"
    when APointerOfAnyOtherTypeIsFiltered
      // former flow: t2-a-pointer-of-any-other-type-is-filtered.moment
      // Outcome: the Pointer is of a type the checks do not admit, so it is filtered and noted, gets no Receipt and finishes.
      // S: citations of the former flow that its nodes do not repeat (kept, none dropped):
      // carried from the former flow, T2.M2 · The gate admits it: the gate reads the latest SiftEnabled or SiftDisabled directly and records its decision (admitted, refused, filtered, Postponed or no-op), before RecordReceipt  // S:294 "records its decision (RecordGateDecision, GateDecisionRecorded). The key of RecordGateDecision is the unit of work plus the decision ordinal"
      // carried from the former flow, T2.M2 · The gate admits it: note enablement: "The gate reads the latest SiftEnabled or SiftDisabled recorded on SiftEnablement, directly, when the work is taken"  // S:294 "the gate reads the latest SiftEnabled or SiftDisabled recorded on SiftEnablement, directly"
      // T2.M3·B1 · when the Pointer is of any other type
      // when the Pointer is of any other type: filtered; a filtered entry is noted (an operational record, never domain state) and finishes; it gets no Receipt  // S:367 "A filtered entry is noted (§7) and finishes; it gets no Receipt (P29-S1)."
      design: RecordGateDecision  // S:1410 "RecordGateDecision | the hard-stop gate, when work is taken"
      design: GateDecisionRecorded [outcome]  // S:1352 "GateDecisionRecorded | StartCycle (an Admitted decision starts the Cycle); the refusal notice (§1 Hard-stop gate, Refusal notices)"
    when AWriteMadeOnSiftsOwnConnectionIsNeverAdmitted
      // former flow: t2-a-write-made-on-sifts-own-connection-is-never-admitted.moment
      // Outcome: the Pointer is for a write made on Sift's own connection, so the self-write guard filters it.
      // T2.M3·B2 · when the Pointer is a write made on Sift's own connection
      // when the Pointer is a write made on Sift's own connection: never admitted (R28-A1, ruling 0209636d); noted; it gets no Receipt  // S:367 "the self-write guard (the Pointer for a write made on Sift's own connection is never admitted"
      design: RecordGateDecision  // S:1410 "RecordGateDecision | the hard-stop gate, when work is taken"
      design: GateDecisionRecorded [outcome]  // S:1352 "GateDecisionRecorded | StartCycle (an Admitted decision starts the Cycle); the refusal notice (§1 Hard-stop gate, Refusal notices)"
    when PostponedWorkIsRefusedWhenSiftIsDisabledMeanwhile
      // former flow: t2-postponed-work-is-refused-when-sift-is-disabled-meanwhile.moment
      // S: citations of the former flow that its nodes do not repeat (kept, none dropped):
      // carried from the former flow, its description: description "T2 — Gated work that waits for the customer workspace to be ready is refused as Refused{Disabled} when Sift is disabled meanwhile, and its submitter is told. Spec of record S:351."
      // T2.M4·B1 · when the workspace is not ready and Sift is disabled meanwhile
      // gated work waits until the customer workspace is ready; if Sift is disabled meanwhile, that work is refused and its submitter told (a notice is not a declared event)  // S:351 "if Sift is disabled meanwhile, that work is refused as Refused{Disabled} and its submitter told"
      design: RecordGateDecision  // S:1410 "RecordGateDecision | the hard-stop gate, when work is taken"
      design: GateDecisionRecorded [terminal]  // S:1352 "GateDecisionRecorded | StartCycle (an Admitted decision starts the Cycle); the refusal notice (§1 Hard-stop gate, Refusal notices)"
    when SiftIsDisabledAndTheGateRefusesTheEntry
      // former flow: t2-sift-is-disabled-and-the-gate-refuses-the-entry.moment
      // Outcome: Sift is disabled, so every user ingress is refused with the disable cause, with no Receipt.
      // T2.M2·B1 · when Sift is disabled
      // when Sift is disabled: all user ingress is refused with the disable cause (LicenseLapsed or Suspended); no Receipt (the gate runs before RecordReceipt)  // S:295 "it refuses all user ingress (a gate refusal)"
      // a notice to Live arrivals that the entry is waiting for Sift to be re-enabled, only once a SiftEnabled or SiftDisabled is recorded (a poster side effect: not declarable)  // S:297 "for Entries, only Live arrivals get a notice, and only once a SiftEnabled or SiftDisabled is recorded"
      // Sift comes back in T8  // S:302 "the enablement path: entitlement observations and EnableSift(Person) requests, including the setup and its Replay that run inside them"
      design: RecordGateDecision  // S:1410 "RecordGateDecision | the hard-stop gate, when work is taken"
      design: GateDecisionRecorded [terminal]  // S:1352 "GateDecisionRecorded | StartCycle (an Admitted decision starts the Cycle); the refusal notice (§1 Hard-stop gate, Refusal notices)"
    when TheWorkspaceIsNotReadySoTheWorkIsPostponed
      // former flow: t2-the-workspace-is-not-ready-so-the-work-is-postponed.moment
      // Outcome: the customer workspace is not ready, so the gated work is Postponed; it is admitted when ready and refused with a notice if Sift is disabled meanwhile (NDD: returns-to T2.M2).
      // T2.M4·B1 · when the workspace is not ready
      // when the workspace is not ready: the work is Postponed (never "Deferred", which is a Placement state); admitted when ready; refused, with its submitter told, if Sift is disabled meanwhile  // S:351 "gated work that arrives before the customer workspace is ready waits until it is ready; if Sift is disabled meanwhile, that work is refused as Refused{Disabled} and its submitter told"
      design: RecordGateDecision  // S:1410 "RecordGateDecision | the hard-stop gate, when work is taken"
      design: GateDecisionRecorded [outcome]  // S:1352 "GateDecisionRecorded | StartCycle (an Admitted decision starts the Cycle); the refusal notice (§1 Hard-stop gate, Refusal notices)"

  moment "T2.M3 · Chatter is filtered at the door"
    // Cheap checks with no content: the type from the Pointer (decision.*, exploration.*, the session-boundary kind, the answer kind) and the self-write guard; this Pointer passes both  // S:367 "the type from the Pointer (decision.*, exploration.*, the session-boundary kind"
    note intake: "Cheap checks, with no content: the type from the Pointer (decision.*, exploration.*, the session-boundary kind, the answer kind) and the self-write guard"  // S:367 "the type from the Pointer"

  moment "T2.M4 · It is received"
    // Prerequisite: the customer workspace is ready, else Postponed (T2.M4·B1); one Receipt per Pointer, the first Arrival wins  // S:368 "**Prerequisite:** Postponed if the customer workspace isn't ready."
    intake: RecordReceipt  // S:369 "**RecordReceipt(Pointer, Arrival).**"

  moment "T2.M5 · It is read and handed on" [branch]
    intake: ReceiptRecorded  // S:321 "ReceiptRecorded {Arrival};"
    when TheMainPath
      // the main path of the story: no node here, the deciding event is the plain node above; the main path goes on in the moment that follows (founder ruling "Yes, anchor the branches": the deciding event is moved into the branch moment, the arm carries none of the main path's nodes)
    when ASessionEndsAndTheQuestionsArriveTogether
      // former flow: t2-a-session-ends-and-the-questions-arrive-together.moment
      // T2.M6 · A session ends and the questions arrive together
      // [flmnt] a keyframe.written or session.recap entry: the session boundary  // S:145 "a feed entry of the boundary kind (flmnt's keyframe.written or session.recap"
      // a boundary entry runs no Extraction: its Cycle runs the question sweep (S:1100), then flushes the gathered postings of this customer workspace (one post per base subject), then MarkProcessed  // S:373 "**A session-boundary entry** (Round 15, ruling 1) runs no Extraction"
      // the sweep and the flush are steps of the Cycle, not commands; a replayed boundary entry runs the sweep and posts nothing, its postings wait for the Replay's one flush  // S:1100 "a replayed boundary entry runs the sweep and posts nothing"
      // MarkProcessed is the unit of work's last command for every entry (T2.M7); a boundary entry carries the effect None(boundary), drawn here because the thread places it at T2.M6  // S:373 "then MarkProcessed (effect None(boundary))"
      intake: MarkProcessed  // S:373 "then MarkProcessed (effect None(boundary))"
      intake: ReceiptProcessed [outcome]  // S:322 "ReceiptProcessed {effect: Applied | None(reason)};"
    when TheEntryYieldsNoCandidate
      // former flow: t2-the-entry-yields-no-candidate.moment
      // Outcome: Extraction yields no candidate, so no MatchCandidate is issued and the Receipt is processed with effect None(no candidate) (NDD: returns-to T2.M7).
      // T2.M5·B1 · when the entry yields no candidate
      // when the entry yields no candidate: no MatchCandidate, no Placement; the unit of work ends with MarkProcessed (effect None(no candidate))  // S:373 "none for an entry that yields none"
      intake: MarkProcessed  // S:317 "MarkProcessed(effect?);"
      intake: ReceiptProcessed [outcome]  // S:322 "ReceiptProcessed {effect: Applied | None(reason)};"
    when TheSourceAlreadyHasAScopeTombstone
      // former flow: t2-the-source-already-has-a-scope-tombstone.moment
      // Outcome: the entry's source already has a scope tombstone, so the Receipt is recorded and closed at dispatch and the work is never started; continues in T7.N1.
      // T2.M4·B3 · when the source already has a scope tombstone
      // when the source already has a scope tombstone: RecordReceipt, then CloseReceipt(erased) in a Cycle of its own; the work of an erased source is never started; a model-wide pass of the closure follows, outside a Replay and an intake  // S:372 "→ RecordReceipt, then CloseReceipt(erased): the Receipt is closed at dispatch, the work of an erased source is never started"
      intake: CloseReceipt  // S:319 "CloseReceipt(erased)."
      intake: ReceiptClosed  // S:326 "ReceiptClosed {erased}."
      design: RecordPassTrigger  // S:341 "RecordPassTrigger is issued by the Cycle's settle step"
      // the Cycle's settle step issues it, once for each attempt, with one cause by precedence (a step, not a policy; cause ClosedAtDispatch)  // S:341 "ClosedAtDispatch applies when the Cycle recorded the closure of a Receipt whose source already has a scope tombstone"
      design: PassTriggerRecorded  // S:341 "each model-wide pass of a Receipt's redo, of an erasure and of a closure at dispatch is started on a PassTriggerRecorded"
      design: StartPass  // S:341 "A policy on PassTriggerRecorded issues StartPass(Convergence, model-wide)"
        triggered-by PassTriggerRecorded  // S:341 "A policy on PassTriggerRecorded issues StartPass(Convergence, model-wide)" (policy PassTriggerRecordedStartsConvergencePass)
      design: PassStarted [outcome]  // S:672 "PassStarted {startPosition, CorpusVersion, RulesVersion}"
      // T2.H1 · continues in T7.N1 (handoff)

  moment "T2.M5 · It is read and handed on (main path)"
    // the main path of the story
    // Otherwise run the Cycle (CycleStarted first, then NodeChanged per write). By kind: a feed decision -> Extraction then MatchCandidate (T3); decision.superseded first runs the waiver check, RevokeWaiver per active waiver (T15.M3); an `answer` Pointer -> ResolveQuestion (T4.M4); an erasure-stream entry -> ReadModelDestruction (T7); a boundary entry -> T2.M6  // S:373 "feed: for a decision.superseded entry first the waiver check, then Extraction"
    design: StartCycle  // S:958 "StartCycle(trigger: CycleTrigger, decision: RecordRef, attempt, redrives?, replayPoint?, endPoint?);"
      triggered-by GateDecisionRecorded  // S:982 "An Admitted decision is followed by StartCycle" (policy AdmittedGateDecisionStartsCycle)
    design: CycleStarted  // S:902 "**StartCycle**(trigger: CycleTrigger, decision: RecordRef, attempt, redrives?, replayPoint?, endPoint?) (NEW) records **CycleStarted** {CycleId, trigger: CycleTrigger, decision: RecordRef, attempt, redrives?, replayPoint?, endPoint?} first, for every Cycle that starts."
    design: MatchCandidate  // S:373 "Extraction (§3 Placement; Round 13) issues MatchCandidate(Pointer, Fingerprint, Arrival) once per candidate the entry yields"

  moment "T2.M7 · The unit of work is complete"
    design: CompleteCycle  // S:959 "CompleteCycle(outcome, failedCommands?, ingressEffect?, constructStates, designState, position);"

  moment "T2.M7 · The unit of work is complete (continued)" [branch]
    design: CycleCompleted  // S:344 "**MarkProcessed(effect)** is the unit of work's last command, issued after CycleCompleted{Succeeded} is recorded"
    when TheMainPath
      // the main path of the story: no node here, the deciding event is the plain node above; the main path goes on in the moment that follows (founder ruling "Yes, anchor the branches": the deciding event is moved into the branch moment, the arm carries none of the main path's nodes)
    when MarkProcessedFails
      // former flow: t2-mark-processed-fails.moment
      // Outcome: MarkProcessed fails, so the entry is not processed and the failure is a failed attempt of the unit of work; continues in T9.M1.
      // T2.M7 · The unit of work is complete
      intake: MarkProcessed  // S:344 "If MarkProcessed fails, the entry is not processed and the failure is a failed attempt of the unit of work"
      // T2.M7·B1 · when MarkProcessed fails
      // when MarkProcessed fails: the entry is not processed; the failure is a failed attempt (RecordFailedAttempt), so the Receipt is failed and open, counts toward the bound and is redone like any failed entry by the next live arrival  // S:344 "so that the Receipt is failed and open, counts toward the bound and is redone like any failed entry by the next live arrival"
      intake: RecordFailedAttempt  // S:345 "RecordFailedAttempt(cycleId, Pointer, Arrival)** is issued when an entry's processing fails (a failed MarkProcessed included)"
      intake: AttemptFailed [terminal]  // S:323 "AttemptFailed {cycleId, attempt, quarantined};"
      // T2.H2 · continues in T9.M1 (handoff)

  moment "T2.M7 · The unit of work is complete (continued, main path)"
    // the main path of the story
    // MarkProcessed is the unit of work's last command, issued after CycleCompleted{Succeeded} is recorded
    intake: MarkProcessed  // S:317 "MarkProcessed(effect?);"
      triggered-by CycleCompleted  // S:344 "is the unit of work's last command, issued after CycleCompleted{Succeeded} is recorded" (policy CycleCompletedMarksProcessed)
    intake: ReceiptProcessed [terminal]  // S:322 "ReceiptProcessed {effect: Applied | None(reason)};"

  moment "T2.O2 · A decision reached Sift (terminal)"
    // PROVES: ReceiptRecorded -> CycleCompleted{Succeeded} -> ReceiptProcessed {Applied | None(...)} for the Pointer; nothing for chatter (the filtered flows)  // S:373 "effect Applied when any command ran in the Cycle"
    note design: "The convergence read model folds the recorded events into the baseline and the inputs of the verdict"  // S:1299 "convergence read model (a failed-and-open Receipt ends)"
